7184	{"artifactId":"LLD-d27fe8996fc3a2db-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-d27fe8996fc3a2db-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:30:06.468Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the request (reuse an existing non-chat group; otherwise today's placement; quiet opens keep focus in the chat) and builds no non-goal (other panels such as the delivery board stay at ViewColumn.Active).","evidence":"Sections 2.1/3.2/6 state all three behaviours; extension.ts:762 (delivery board, ViewColumn.Active) and the status panel are explicitly left unchanged ('Only the review pane is changed'). ac1-ac3 are derived from the request (open question ts1 says so) and each maps to a stated behaviour. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the review host's createPanel opens at ViewColumn.Beside with preserveFocus when quiet, else ViewColumn.Active.","evidence":"extension.ts:719-721: `const panel = quiet === true ? vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(viewType, title, { viewColumn: vscode.ViewColumn.Beside, preserveFocus: true }, ...) : vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(viewType, title, vscode.ViewColumn.Active, ...)`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An already open pane is only revealed; createPanel is called only when the host has no live pane.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.ts:2351-2360 show(quiet): reveals the existing channel (with preserveFocus when quiet) and only otherwise calls deps.createPanel({ viewType, title, ...(quiet ? { quiet: true } : {}) }). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The vscode.d.ts shim today declares only TabGroup.activeTab and TabGroups.activeTabGroup/onDidChangeTabs/onDidChangeTabGroups.","evidence":"vscode.d.ts:95-108: Tab { input }, TabGroup { activeTab }, TabGroups { activeTabGroup; onDidChangeTabs; onDidChangeTabGroups } - no `all`, `viewColumn`, `isActive` or `tabs`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/vscode.d.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"isChatTabInput(input: unknown, viewType: string): boolean exists in group-lock.ts with the stated shape and rejects non-object or viewType-less inputs.","evidence":"group-lock.ts:49-54: returns false when `typeof input !== 'object' || input === null` or viewType is not a string; else `actual === viewType || actual.endsWith(`-${viewType}`)`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/group-lock.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"chooseReviewColumn / review-column.ts do not already exist.","evidence":"No review-column.ts under vscode-plugin/src/chat; extension.ts reads tabGroups only for activeTabGroup.activeTab and the change events (extension.ts:552-555). [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Two source scans in review-wiring.test.ts pin the current createPanel calls and must be rewritten, and their extractor regex expects the `createPanel: ({ viewType, title, quiet }) => {` block shape.","evidence":"review-wiring.test.ts:125 and :173 extract with /createPanel: \\(\\{ viewType, title, quiet \\}\\) => \\{([\\s\\S]*?)\\n      \\},/; :128 asserts the ViewColumn.Active call; :175 asserts the quiet Beside/preserveFocus ternary; :144 title states the old placement. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/review-wiring.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CHAT_VIEW_TYPE is available in extension.ts for the createPanel callback to pass to chooseReviewColumn.","evidence":"extension.ts:52 imports CHAT_VIEW_TYPE from './chat/chat-panel.js' and :551 already uses it for the group lock. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored data or message shape changes; only where a new review pane opens.","evidence":"The createPanel dep signature (docs-review-panel.ts:36) is unchanged; the change is inside the extension.ts callback and a new pure function; nothing is persisted. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed read of tabGroups is caught and falls back to today's placement; non-object tab inputs do not mark a group as the chat's.","evidence":"Section 4 states a try around the tabGroups.all read with logging and the Beside/Active fallback; isChatTabInput (group-lock.ts:50-52) already returns false for non-object or missing-viewType inputs, so the second case needs no new code. extension.ts has panelLog for the log. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/group-lock.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each derived criterion ac1-ac3 maps to a test: pure-function unit tests over fake groups (as group-lock.test.ts does) plus rewritten source scans for the wiring and focus.","evidence":"Section 5 acceptance mapping covers ac1 (review-column.test.ts active-first), ac2 (undefined + source-scan fallback), ac3 (source-scan preserveFocus). group-lock.test.ts exists as the fake-based precedent; review-wiring.test.ts already uses source scans of the same createPanel block. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/group-lock.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/review-wiring.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T19:30:06.468Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
